COâ\n4. Borman Describes View of Earth from Midway to Moon\n5. Communications Prior to LOI (Lunar Orbit Insertion) to LOS\n6. First Communications After LOI\n7. Lovell Describes View of Earth from Lunar Orbit; Color of Water & Land Areas; Weather\n8. âApollo 8, Live from The Moonâ Sequence; Commentary by Crew on Moonâs Appearance; âVast Forboding,â, etcetera.\n9. Christmas Eve Service; Genesis Reading by All Crew Members\n10. Communications Prior to Trans-Earth Injection (TEI) from 3 Minutes Till Loss of Signal\n11. âThere Is A Santa Claus;â Lovell Comments After TEI Burn\n12. Pre-Separation Communications; âPyro-Armâ Sequence\n13. âReal Fireball;â Re-Entry\n14. Post-Splashdown Commentary Relaying Crew-Recovery Conversations; Includes âAmerican Cheeseâ Comment\n15. President Johnson Phones Congratulations to Crew on Recovery Ship\n\nDigitized, cataloged and archived by the Houston Audio Control Room, at the NASA Johnson Space Center.","subject":"NASA; Audio Highlight Reels","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/","publicdate":"2010-11-29 15:38:01","addeddate":"2010-11-29 15:30:47","uploader":"john.l.stoll@nasa.gov","updater":["John Stoll","John Stoll","John Stoll","John Stoll","John Stoll"],"updatedate":["2010-11-29 16:03:57","2010-11-30 16:50:15","2010-12-07 15:05:38","2010-12-07 15:38:08","2010-12-09 16:15:48"],"boxid":"OL100020401","backup_location":"ia903607_21"},"server":"ia600603.us.archive.org","uniq":1880329610,"workable_servers":["ia600603.us.archive.org","ia800603.us.archive.org"]}